,"References",null],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"doc":1,"prev":8,"next":11},{"slug":2,"num":3,"title":4,"html":5,"toc":6,"summary":7},"requirements",3,"Requirements","\u003Cp>On your computer:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Go 1.27 or later, to build the tool.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Node.js 22.17 or later, to build the web console. CI uses Node.js 24 LTS.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>An \u003Ccode>ssh\u003C/code> client. The \u003Ccode>backup\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>db\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>adopt\u003C/code>, and \u003Ccode>monitor install\u003C/code> commands use it.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>An SSH key pair. The default public key path is \u003Ccode>~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>Or only Docker. The \u003Ca href=\"/pgha-cli/docs/container-image/\">container image\u003C/a> has pgha, the\nweb console and the \u003Ccode>ssh\u003C/code> client.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>At Hetzner:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>A Hetzner Cloud project.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>An API token with \u003Cstrong>Read &amp; Write\u003C/strong> permission.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>Optional:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>An S3 bucket and access key, for backups.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A Tailscale auth key, for \u003Ccode>--tailscale\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>An HTTPS webhook URL, for alerts.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[],"On your computer:",{"slug":9,"title":10},"architecture","Architecture",{"slug":12,"title":13},"install","Install"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
